+# Compatibility research record
+
+Consulted 2026-08-15 using live network access.
+
+- **Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability — checked the published matrix surface used to evaluate vCenter, ESXi, and NSX combinations. It confirmed that interoperability is a separate concern from whether a direct product upgrade is a supported VCF workflow.
+- **Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html — used for the 9.1 route from a vCenter/ESXi 8.x estate with NSX 4.x: use VCF Installer conversion/import; independent component upgrades are not offered when NSX is present.
+- **Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html — used for the core lifecycle order of SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, and ESXi. In this task the management domain is already at target, leaving NSX before vCenter before the ESXi/vSAN image for the imported workload domain.
+- **vCenter upgrade precheck from version 8.x to 9.x failing due to NSX version** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/425164/vcenter-upgrade-precheck-from-version-8x.html — used to reject a standalone vCenter-first move while NSX remains on 4.2.2.1 and to route the existing NSX deployment through VCF workload-domain management first.
+- **Upgrading a Brownfield-imported domain fails during the upgrade pre-check phase due to an unsupported upgrade path for NSX** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430524/upgrading-a-brownfieldimported-domain-fa.html — used to distinguish the earlier 9.0.1 failure for NSX 4.2.3.3 from the documented option to wait for the 9.1 line that supports that NSX path.
